   "conclusion": {
    "diagnosis": "CNC-02 is showing intermittent vibration exceeding the 4.50 mm/s threshold: alarms at tick 914 (4.58 mm/s) and tick 919 (4.51 mm/s), with readings below threshold in between (915–918, 920). Load is stable (~53–57%, E6), so this is not load-driven process variation. No prior alarms before 914 (E3, E7), so this is a new/developing pattern rather than a one-off transient (H1) or long-standing variation (H4). A sensor fault (H3) is not ruled out but unsupported. The pattern best fits H2: a developing mechanical issue causing repeated threshold exceedances that may recur or escalate. Confidence is about 0.85, below the 0.90 needed to intervene. One more check — spindle temperature during the same window — could confirm a mechanical cause (overheating bearing) and raise confidence to intervene, or support a sensor fault if temperature is normal.",
